- `en_us.json` - all dimension translations

### Key Technical Decisions
- Config uses nested static holders (NetherAtmosphere, EndAtmosphere) not instance wrappers
- V1 scope: 9 settings per dimension (no ambientLight EV)
- SimpleDimensionAtmosphere record holds all 9 values
- skyPush() builds effective values BEFORE SkyPush construction (no post-hoc patching)
- Separated signatures: lastSkyParameterSignature (LUT), lastRenderedSkyParameterSignature (miss shader)
- Dimension tab switching resets scroll via pendingAtmosphereContentReset flag (not rememberMenuPosition)
- Lower-horizon protection in rmiss: smoothstep(-1e-3, 0, dir.y) blend to groundVoid

### Build Status
- BLOCKED: Requires Slang 2026.13 compiler (CAUSTICA_SLANGC env var or -Pslangc=<path>)
- Java compile not reachable until build.gradle configuration passes

### Lessons Learned
- Plan document provides detailed code snippets and file paths
- Config structure decisions have cascading effects (settings screen, tests, ALL[] array)
- Nested static holders are the idiomatic pattern for CausticaConfig settings
- Signature separation is important: LUT invalidation is cheaper than full pipeline reset
- Lower-horizon protection prevents dimension color leaking into underground geometry
